"-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529766} {:answer/id #uuid "59d62063-4fad-511a-b194-efc0b6119dd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529796} {:answer/id #uuid "bf19790b-8756-5eae-a0a9-1c6a110f2908" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530058}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c3458df-575f-5ef2-9d90-cb1036411ba3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529721} :answer-field/id #uuid "70af9fde-fcc8-5bcd-92ba-0039303dd725" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530304}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f6d25fc7-2826-55d4-8ca7-6baff343a22b" :question/math-academy-id "q-154915" :question/problem "If ${a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}-3$ with ${a}_{1}=-1,$ then ${a}_{3}=$" :question/worked-solution "The recursive formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}-3,\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}=-1.$\n\nWe use this formula to compute the terms ${a}_{2}$ and ${a}_{3}$ as follows:\n\n- We first compute ${a}_{2}$ by substituting $n=1$ into the recursive formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n+1} & ={a}_{n}-3 \\\\ {a}_{1+1} & ={a}_{1}-3 \\\\ {a}_{2} & ={a}_{1}-3 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =(-1)-3 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we compute ${a}_{3}$ by substituting $n=2$ into the recursive formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n+1} & ={a}_{n}-3 \\\\ {a}_{2+1} & ={a}_{2}-3 \\\\ {a}_{3} & ={a}_{2}-3 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =(-4)-3 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${a}_{3}=-7.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530455 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100880 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0fbdcd5f-41de-52fa-9652-3084a5edc01f" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Second Term of a Sequence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eab261b7-b013-56de-bd9f-08c2f4da9266" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530166}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eab261b7-b013-56de-bd9f-08c2f4da9266" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530166} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe27cd55-d639-5c22-8152-3b7caa207a64" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530411}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "505d1135-d7f1-5121-9de9-d7f356adef17" :question/math-academy-id "q-214107" :question/problem "If ${a}_{n+1}=2-5{a}_{n}$ with ${a}_{1}=-3,$ then ${a}_{2}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The recursive formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=2-5{a}_{n}\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}=-3.$\n\nWe compute ${a}_{2}$ by substituting $n=1$ into the recursive formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n+1} & =2-5{a}_{n} \\\\ {a}_{1+1} & =2-5{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2} & =2-5{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2} & =2-5(-3) \\\\ {a}_{2} & =17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${a}_{2}=17.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530428 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100883 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a1bf68a-bdb3-5e76-a587-ff0abdae982f" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Recursive Formula for a Sequence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd715190-2938-5e32-a961-819d9c3e139c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530127}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd715190-2938-5e32-a961-819d9c3e139c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530127} :answer-field/id #uuid "9934f2fa-e6e1-55cd-aa47-e6f08f613509" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530330} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a55c831e-b121-50d2-add0-8419e55c5f42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529991}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a55c831e-b121-50d2-add0-8419e55c5f42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529991} :answer-field/id #uuid "fcc44002-16a0-5a8f-8c9d-ff051caefb39" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530410}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1af1950b-cdfe-5acc-bf2c-2c2896e4be38" :question/math-academy-id "q-214169" :question/problem "Consider the following sequence: \n\n$$\n5,\\,1,\\,-3,\\,-7,\\,-11,\\,…\n$$\n\nThe recursive formula for this sequence is given by \n\n${a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}\\,-$\n{{field-1}}, \n$\\,{a}_{1}=$ \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the first term of the sequence is ${a}_{1}=5.$\n\nInspecting the terms of the sequence, we see that we always get the next term by subtracting $4.$\n\nTherefore, the recursive rule must be the following:\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}-4\\,,\\,{a}_{1}=5\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530416 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100882 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e74655b8-92bc-5142-96b7-408643c8ad39" :knowledge-point/title "Recursive Sequences in Function Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96a97928-ad4e-547a-9983-6109cd4541be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529947}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "96a97928-ad4e-547a-9983-6109cd4541be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529947} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd33b480-aac6-50ef-a0cb-339fb8ae8ddf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530370}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "04239873-7b65-5dcb-9652-60e8fa1e2863" :question/math-academy-id "q-217117" :question/problem "If $f(n+1)=7-3f(n)$ with $f(1)=1,$ then $f(3)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The recursive formula is\n\n$$\nf(n+1)=7-3f(n),\n$$\n\nwhere $f(1)=1.$\n\nWe use this formula to compute the terms $f(2)$ and $f(3)$ as follows:\n\n- To compute $f(2),$ we substitute $n=1$ into the recursive formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(n+1) & =7-3f(n) \\\\ f(1+1) & =7-3f(1) \\\\ f(2) & =7-3f(1) \\\\ f(2) & =7-3(1) \\\\ f(2) & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To compute $f(3),$ we substitute $n=2$ into the recursive formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(n+1) & =7-3f(n) \\\\ f(2+1) & =7-3f(2) \\\\ f(3) & =7-3f(2) \\\\ f(3) & =7-3(4) \\\\ f(3) & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(3)=-5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530429 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100883 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a1bf68a-bdb3-5e76-a587-ff0abdae982f" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Recursive Formula for a Sequence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f44cb58-7ab7-5375-8a41-094167fa1753" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f44cb58-7ab7-5375-8a41-094167fa1753" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529647} :answer-field/id #uuid "17904481-0ffc-50ed-85b0-0db14565fd49" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530233} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb25a4ca-b71b-5331-94ed-6c82149721b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530203}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb25a4ca-b71b-5331-94ed-6c82149721b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530203} :answer-field/id #uuid "edf21408-0ddd-554b-bb71-b0725cb2b8d4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530390}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1b0f3ebd-62a2-5a4c-a297-4baeb4f4a880" :question/math-academy-id "q-217143" :question/problem "Consider the following sequence: \n\n$$\n3,\\,6,\\,12,\\,24,\\,48,\\,…\n$$\n\nThe recursive formula for this sequence is given by\n\n${a}_{n+1}=$\n{{field-1}}$\\cdot \\,{a}_{n},$ \n$\\,{a}_{1}=$ \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the first term of the sequence is ${a}_{1}=3.$\n\nInspecting the terms of the sequence, we see that we always get the next term by multiplying by $2.$\n\nTherefore, the recursive rule must be the following:\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=2\\cdot {a}_{n}\\,,\\,{a}_{1}=3\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530476 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100882 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e74655b8-92bc-5142-96b7-408643c8ad39" :knowledge-point/title "Recursive Sequences in Function Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "011924fd-f3c4-5782-bf54-f04b32df2b61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529576} {:answer/id #uuid "39c4e8c3-5559-5867-a4b5-f8f7f2ac1cc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529713} {:answer/id #uuid "4e95ec65-e2ae-539c-ae7d-97088f876913" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-162" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529769} {:answer/id #uuid "890bad82-2880-5fc8-9f51-ab781aa15b05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529914} {:answer/id #uuid "9fe6f239-8950-5dbb-bec9-d36ec604e430" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529975}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9fe6f239-8950-5dbb-bec9-d36ec604e430" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529975} :answer-field/id #uuid "4974fa16-432b-51f1-a65b-e3112a7e1f6f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530272}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "71cd7479-8b84-567f-a02b-5eec2ad87d28" :question/math-academy-id "q-51885" :question/problem "If $f(n+1)=3f(n)$ with $f(1)=-2,$ then $f(4)=$" :question/worked-solution "The recursive formula is\n\n$$\nf(n+1)=3f(n),\n$$\n\nwhere $f(1)=-2.$\n\nWe use this formula to compute the terms $f(2),f(3),$ and $f(4)$ as follows:\n\n- To compute $f(2),$ we substitute $n=1$ into the recursive formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(n+1) & =3f(n) \\\\ f(1+1) & =3f(1) \\\\ f(2) & =3f(1) \\\\ f(2) & =3(-2) \\\\ f(2) & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To compute $f(3),$ we substitute $n=2$ into the recursive formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(n+1) & =3f(n) \\\\ f(2+1) & =3f(2) \\\\ f(3) & =3f(2) \\\\ f(3) & =3(-6) \\\\ f(3) & =-18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To compute $f(4),$ we substitute $n=3$ into the recursive formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(n+1) & =3f(n) \\\\ f(3+1) & =3f(3) \\\\ f(4) & =3f(3) \\\\ f(4) & =3(-18) \\\\ f(4) & =-54\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fourth term of the sequence is $f(4)=-54.$"}]}
